### 慳1 | _(1)H(a/)n_ [[haan1]]

$$
R
  ⼼ + 11
U
  U+6173
A
  ==
  - 悭 (Mainland simplified)
  ==
F
  ==
  - (F2.67 慳) 香閒切吝嗇也
  ==
W
  ====
  - [[Page~72 (1)慳]]
    ==
    - Saving, niggardly, stingy;
    - to be sparing of;
    - _(1)h(a/)n k(i/)m(6)_
        [[haan1 gim6 慳儉]]
        parsimonious, close;
    - _(1)h(a/)n lun(6)_ [[haan1 leon6 慳吝]]
        ~~(or _nun(6)_ [[neon6]])~~
        stingy;
    - _(1)h(a/)n lik(9)_
        [[haan1 lik6 慳力]]
        saving of strength;
    - _(2)h(o\) (1)h(a/)n_
        [[hou2 haan1 好慳]],
        closefisted;
    - _(1)h(a/)n (1)f(a/)n_
        [[haan1 faan1 慳返]],
        saved the expense, spared the trouble``.``
    ==
  ====
C
  ==
  - In Cantonese, 慳 is usually used positively
    to mean "frugal" rather than "stingy"
    (e.g. in the compliment 知慳識儉).
  ==
E
  ====
  - 【慳】 (haan1)
    ++
    1. To be frugal, to economise.
       ==
       - 慳水 (haan1 seoi2): "Save water."
       - 慳錢 (haan1 cin4-2): "Save money."
       - 慳皮 (haan1 pei4-2): "Be frugal."
       - 慳電膽 (haan1 din6 daam2): "Energy-saving [light]-bulb" (i.e. a compact fluorescent lamp).
       ==
    ++
  ====
$$


